{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Our fathers did not grasp Your wonders</b> — the signs and portents that You did in Egypt." "<b>The multitude of Your kindnesses</b> — upon Israel in the plague of wild beasts and pestilence and hail and darkness and the plague of the firstborn." "<b>They rebelled at the Sea</b> — for they said, \"Is this not the very thing we spoke to you in Egypt?\" (Exodus 14:12), or they refused to cross the sea."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 106, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:43.001067528Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}